In terms of regulatory compliance, we confirm that we are generally compliant with GDPR requirements as we only operate within the EU and do not transfer data outside the EU. Our standard contractual clauses include provisions for data return and destruction upon termination, and we have a no-copyleft GPL contamination policy in place. We will also ensure explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued by the solution, aligning with the requirement that no decision may be automated without explicit validation by an agent.

To address sovereignty constraints, we propose hosting our solution on a European cloud provider such as Outscale (SecNumCloud) or OVHcloud, ensuring no dependency on non-European suppliers. We will also implement measures to mitigate potential risks associated with supplier dependency and ensure that all data hosting is compliant with SecNumCloud or equivalent standards.

