The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. We will ensure that our solution's annual cost of exploitation remains mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority.

To reduce the environmental footprint of our system, we propose leveraging green hosting partners such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, which offer 100% renewable energy and have a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.3 and 1.28 respectively. We will also implement digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching to reduce recomputes by an estimated 20%, and adhering to a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

Our project deployment will follow a structured approach, including phases such as Inception & Design, Pilot / MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support. We will maintain a risk register, review risks bi-weekly, and categorize them into standard risk categories. Our governance tools, such as RAID log, Decision log, Change request process, and Steering committee, will provide a structured approach to managing the project, while our reporting cadence of weekly status reports, monthly steering committee meetings, and quarterly executive reviews will keep stakeholders informed and engaged throughout the deployment and transition process.

